Policy synthetic, version v1

Parameters
  budget: a number from 1 to 10
  mode: one of 'fast', 'slow', 5 (default 'fast')
  threshold: a number from 0.1 to 0.9 in steps of 0.2 (default 0.3)

Decision gate
  1. If params.threshold is at least 0.5 and ai.score is at most 10, choose escalate.
  2. If not (flag is true) or ai.band is not 'a==b>c' and size is above 3, choose hold.
  3. If x is below 2 and label is "<&&>" and not done, choose skip.
  If no rule matches, the decision fails.

Decision lookup
  1. When active is true and region is 'north' and tier is 2, choose fast.
  2. When rate is 0.25 and region is 'south', choose slow.
  Otherwise, choose slow.
